From 5da2d6c85646044032e6c4742f4a83b3e02c2401 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:51:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sessions): ride out owner-discovery stalls on session
 writes; Desktop Retry

A Desktop archive PATCH got 503 "owner_unavailable: control_timeout: Exclusive
maintenance refused ... Drain and stop the gateway, then retry" because the
session-write route did ONE 1.5s read-only identify while the owning gateway's
control loop was briefly blocked (hub journal: loop blocked 1084.8ms; identify
answered in 692.6ms the same second).

Backend (hermes_cli/session_owner_discovery.py, shared by
_mutate_via_gateway_owner and the router's _on_live_owner):
- retry ONLY inaccessible/control_timeout discovery: <=3 attempts of <=1.5s,
  0.25s backoff, one 6s monotonic budget (no attempt with <0.1s left);
- every other verdict is final on the first read (absent keeps the offline
  exclusive path and its lock; auth/protocol/permission/profile refusals are
  never retried); discovery never starts a gateway;
- the mutation is sent at most once; it is never retried server-side;
- an exhausted control_timeout is a retryable 503 with no drain/stop advice.

Desktop:
- archive and rename failures restore the row and offer Retry only while the
  mutation client retains the intent (shared isDefinitiveSessionMutationRefusal),
  so a Retry replays the same request_id/expected revision;
- the archive owner is pinned once (pinSessionWriteOwner); Retry skips
  preflight/deselect and goes to that same connection/profile;
- the selected-row owner rename went through an UNFENCED PATCH (refused as an
  old client); it now uses the fenced renameSession.

Root producer of the control-loop stall remains undetermined (not attributed).
